darling-installer offers a replacement for the OS X Installer and related utilities.

This project is part of Darling and is not intended for standalone use.

Package scripts execute from their validated extraction directory with an
absolute script path as argv[0]. This preserves interpreter dispatchers that
select the install phase from the basename of $0. Script names remain relative
archive paths: absolute names and parent components are rejected.

Payload extraction requires a canonical target-volume root. Existing directory
aliases may be traversed only when they resolve inside that root. Symlinks
created by the archive cannot become parents, including indirectly through an
existing alias and when the target volume is `/`. Script archives retain their
own narrower extraction root. Absolute archive names and parent traversal are
rejected before extraction.

This is archive-path containment, not a sandbox for package scripts or a lock
against concurrent destination mutations; the caller owns extraction lifecycle.

